  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, increasing gravity causes the actual state of the bones to differ from the intended rest state of the bones, even when the avatar is fully upright. It would be preferable to behave more like pull when the bone in question is at its initial world orientation, and to behave like gravity as it is deflected from that orientation.\nI built a proof-of-concept to test this behavior in editor and it seemed to work well: https://gist.github.com/bdunderscore/23d6b110429132dc78c1e68adfc57cbc (obviously this won't work in client)\nDemo here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R2zOW_uW_Yo\nThis simply interpolates between gravity and pull depending on deflection from the initial orientation. It might be that some kind of non-linear blend would look better, but for now as a proof-of-concept this seems promising.",
